---
import '../../styles/global.css';
import model from '../../../model/dynamos-v2.json';
import precepta from '../../../model/precepta.json';
import researchBackend from '../../../model/research/backend.json';

const rawBase = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const base = rawBase.endsWith('/') ? rawBase : `${rawBase}/`;

const allPatterns = precepta.domains.flatMap((domain) =>
  domain.patterns.map((pattern) => ({
    id: pattern.id,
    name: pattern.name,
    domainName: domain.name,
  }))
);

const researchConfig = {
  apiBase: (researchBackend.api_base ?? '').replace(/\/$/, ''),
  modelVersion: model.version,
  questionnaireVersion: '1.1.0-pilot',
  derivationVersion: '0.3.0-pilot',
  patterns: allPatterns,
};
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="description" content="Live DYNAMOS research status and participant recognition evidence." />
    <title>Research Status — DYNAMOS</title>
  </head>

  <body>
    <header class="site-header">
      <a class="wordmark" href={base}>DYNAMOS</a>
      <nav aria-label="Primary navigation">
        <a href={`${base}model/`}>Model</a>
        <a href={`${base}precepta/`}>PRECEPTA</a>
        <a href={`${base}explore/`}>Explore</a>
        <a aria-current="page" href={`${base}research/`}>Research</a>
        <a href={`${base}faq/`}>FAQ</a>
        <a href={`${base}responsible-use/`}>Responsible use</a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main>
      <section class="research-hero">
        <p class="eyebrow">Open model development · live pilot</p>
        <h1>Help us improve the model.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          DYNAMOS makes higher-order claims from a 26-dimensional self-report.
          Research begins when people tell us whether those claims actually fit.
        </p>

        <div class="research-callout">
          <strong>Agreement is useful. Disagreement is useful. Missing patterns are useful.</strong>
          <span>
            The goal is not to prove DYNAMOS right. It is to discover where its
            derivation rules work, where they fail, and what they do not yet measure.
          </span>
        </div>

        <div class="research-actions">
          <a class="primary-link" href={`${base}explore/`}>Donate your data to research →</a>
          <a class="text-link" href="#how">How contribution works ↓</a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="research-dashboard">
        <div class="dashboard-heading">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Live research status</p>
            <h2>Current pilot cohort</h2>
          </div>
          <p id="research-updated" class="dashboard-updated">Loading live data…</p>
        </div>

        <div class="big-stats" aria-live="polite">
          <article><strong id="research-profile-count">—</strong><span>contributed profiles</span></article>
          <article><strong id="research-judgment-count">—</strong><span>PRECEPTA judgments</span></article>
          <article><strong id="research-overall-fit">—</strong><span>strong / mostly overall recognition</span></article>
          <article><strong>0.3</strong><span>derivation pilot</span></article>
        </div>

        <div class="version-strip">
          <span>Model <strong>2.0.0</strong></span>
          <span>Questionnaire <strong>1.1.0-pilot</strong></span>
          <span>Derivation <strong>0.3.0-pilot</strong></span>
        </div>

        <p id="research-small-sample" class="small-sample-note">
          Overall recognition percentages are withheld until at least 10 contributed
          profiles are available in this exact version cohort.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="research-evidence">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="eyebrow">Pattern-level evidence</p>
          <h2>Which PRECEPTA patterns are holding up?</h2>
          <p>
            Pattern-level statistics appear only after a pattern has been presented
            often enough to pass the public suppression threshold. Until then, small
            cells remain hidden.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="pattern-evidence" class="pattern-evidence" aria-live="polite">
          <p>Loading pattern-level evidence…</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="how" class="research-how">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">What your contribution tests</p>
          <h2>You are evaluating the model, not yourself.</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="research-steps">
          <article>
            <span>01</span>
            <h3>Describe your architecture</h3>
            <p>You answer 26 comparative self-report items. Those responses are the input vector; DYNAMOS does not ask you to validate the scores you just chose.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span>02</span>
            <h3>Evaluate PRECEPTA</h3>
            <p>DYNAMOS generates higher-order patterns and a whole-profile synthesis. You tell us which interpretations you recognize, reject, or find unclear.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span>03</span>
            <h3>Contribute deliberately</h3>
            <p>Only after reviewing the result do you choose whether to donate the structured research record. You can inspect exactly what will be sent first.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="research-privacy">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Privacy-minimized research</p>
          <h2>We want the pattern, not your identity.</h2>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p>The research record is designed around scores, model output, and structured agreement/disagreement. It does not contain a name, email address, employer, diagnosis, exact location, or free-text biography.</p>
          <p>Contributions are stored privately. The public website receives aggregate statistics only. DYNAMOS remains exploratory, non-diagnostic, and not a validated psychometric instrument.</p>
          <p><a class="text-link" href={`${base}responsible-use/`}>Read the responsible-use statement →</a></p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="research-final-cta">
        <p class="eyebrow">Participate</p>
        <h2>Give DYNAMOS a chance to be wrong.</h2>
        <p>The most valuable contribution may be the one that exposes a rule we need to change.</p>
        <a class="primary-link" href={`${base}explore/`}>Explore your architecture and contribute →</a>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer>
      <div>
        <p><strong>DYNAMOS — Dynamic Neuro-Operational Systems Model</strong><br />© {model.copyright.year} {model.copyright.holder}</p>
        <p>Model and content licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="footer-notice">
        <p><strong>Research status:</strong> descriptive model-development evidence, not diagnostic or psychometric validation.</p>
        <p><a href={`${base}responsible-use/`}>Responsible use →</a></p>
      </div>
    </footer>

    <script
      type="application/json"
      id="research-config"
      set:html={JSON.stringify(researchConfig)}
    ></script>

    <script>
      const config = JSON.parse(document.querySelector('#research-config').textContent);

      function patternMeta(id) {
        return config.patterns.find((pattern) => pattern.id === id) ?? {
          id,
          name: id,
          domainName: 'PRECEPTA',
        };
      }

      function percent(numerator, denominator) {
        return denominator ? Math.round((numerator / denominator) * 100) : 0;
      }

      async function loadResearchStats() {
        const updated = document.querySelector('#research-updated');
        const evidence = document.querySelector('#pattern-evidence');

        if (!config.apiBase) {
          updated.textContent = 'Research collection is not connected.';
          evidence.innerHTML = '<p>Live aggregate statistics are not available yet.</p>';
          return;
        }

        const params = new URLSearchParams({
          model_version: config.modelVersion,
          questionnaire_version: config.questionnaireVersion,
          derivation_version: config.derivationVersion,
        });

        try {
          const response = await fetch(
            `${config.apiBase}/v1/stats?${params.toString()}`,
            { headers: { accept: 'application/json' } }
          );
          if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${response.status}`);
          const stats = await response.json();

          const profiles = Number(stats.total_contributions ?? 0);
          const judgments = Number(stats.total_pattern_judgments ?? 0);

          document.querySelector('#research-profile-count').textContent = profiles.toLocaleString();
          document.querySelector('#research-judgment-count').textContent = judgments.toLocaleString();

          const overall = stats.overall_fit_counts ?? {};
          const answeredOverall =
            Number(overall.strongly_recognize ?? 0) +
            Number(overall.mostly_recognize ?? 0) +
            Number(overall.partly_recognize ?? 0) +
            Number(overall.do_not_recognize ?? 0) +
            Number(overall.do_not_understand ?? 0);

          if (profiles >= 10 && answeredOverall > 0) {
            const recognized =
              Number(overall.strongly_recognize ?? 0) +
              Number(overall.mostly_recognize ?? 0);
            document.querySelector('#research-overall-fit').textContent =
              `${percent(recognized, answeredOverall)}%`;
            document.querySelector('#research-small-sample').textContent =
              'Overall recognition summarizes “strongly” + “mostly” responses in this exact version cohort. It is descriptive fit evidence, not a validity coefficient.';
          }

          const generated = stats.generated_at ? new Date(stats.generated_at) : null;
          updated.textContent = generated && !Number.isNaN(generated.valueOf())
            ? `Updated ${generated.toLocaleString()}`
            : 'Live aggregate data';

          const published = (stats.pattern_stats ?? []).filter((row) => row.published);

          if (!published.length) {
            evidence.innerHTML = `
              <div class="evidence-empty">
                <strong>Pattern-level evidence is still accumulating.</strong>
                <p>The current public threshold is ${Number(stats.suppression_threshold ?? 20)} presentations of a pattern. Small cells stay hidden until that threshold is reached.</p>
              </div>`;
            return;
          }

          const byDomain = new Map();

          for (const row of published) {
            const meta = patternMeta(row.pattern_id);
            if (!byDomain.has(meta.domainName)) byDomain.set(meta.domainName, []);

            const counts = row.recognition_counts ?? {};
            const answered =
              Number(counts.strongly_recognize ?? 0) +
              Number(counts.mostly_recognize ?? 0) +
              Number(counts.partly_recognize ?? 0) +
              Number(counts.do_not_recognize ?? 0) +
              Number(counts.do_not_understand ?? 0);

            const highRecognition =
              Number(counts.strongly_recognize ?? 0) +
              Number(counts.mostly_recognize ?? 0);

            byDomain.get(meta.domainName).push({
              ...row,
              name: meta.name,
              recognitionPercent: percent(highRecognition, answered),
            });
          }

          evidence.innerHTML = [...byDomain.entries()].map(([domain, rows]) => `
            <section class="evidence-domain">
              <p class="eyebrow">${domain}</p>
              <div class="evidence-list">
                ${rows.sort((a, b) => b.n_presented - a.n_presented).map((row) => `
                  <article class="evidence-row">
                    <div><strong>${row.name}</strong><span>n = ${row.n_presented}</span></div>
                    <div><strong>${row.recognitionPercent}%</strong><span>strong / mostly recognize</span></div>
                    <div><strong>${row.n_reported_missing}</strong><span>reported missing</span></div>
                  </article>
                `).join('')}
              </div>
            </section>
          `).join('');
        } catch {
          updated.textContent = 'Live statistics temporarily unavailable.';
          evidence.innerHTML = `
            <div class="evidence-empty">
              <strong>The live research endpoint could not be reached.</strong>
              <p>The questionnaire and local PRECEPTA interpretation still work normally.</p>
            </div>`;
        }
      }

      loadResearchStats();
    </script>

    <style>
      .research-hero { padding: 7rem 2rem 5rem; }

      .research-callout {
        max-width: 860px;
        margin-top: 3rem;
        padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
        border-left: 4px solid currentColor;
        display: grid;
        gap: 0.35rem;
      }

      .research-actions {
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 1rem 1.5rem;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        margin-top: 2.5rem;
      }

      .primary-link {
        display: inline-block;
        padding: 0.8rem 1rem;
        border: 1px solid #17202a;
        border-radius: 0.55rem;
        background: #17202a;
        color: #f7f5ef;
        text-decoration: none;
        font-weight: 750;
      }

      .research-dashboard,
      .research-evidence,
      .research-how,
      .research-privacy,
      .research-final-cta {
        padding: 5rem 2rem;
        border-top: 1px solid #b9b6ad;
      }

      .dashboard-heading {
        display: flex;
        justify-content: space-between;
        gap: 2rem;
        align-items: end;
        margin-bottom: 2rem;
      }

      .dashboard-updated,
      .small-sample-note { font-size: 0.86rem; }

      .big-stats {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
        border-top: 1px solid #b9b6ad;
        border-bottom: 1px solid #b9b6ad;
      }

      .big-stats article { display: grid; padding: 1.5rem 1rem 1.5rem 0; }
      .big-stats strong { font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 5vw, 4rem); line-height: 1; }
      .big-stats span { margin-top: 0.6rem; font-size: 0.82rem; }

      .version-strip {
        display: flex;
        gap: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        padding: 1rem 0;
        font-size: 0.85rem;
      }

      .pattern-evidence { margin-top: 2rem; }

      .evidence-empty {
        max-width: 800px;
        padding: 1.5rem;
        border: 1px solid #b9b6ad;
        border-radius: 0.75rem;
      }

      .evidence-domain { padding: 2rem 0; border-top: 1px solid #d2cfc6; }
      .evidence-list { display: grid; }

      .evidence-row {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: minmax(220px, 2fr) 1fr 1fr;
        gap: 1rem;
        padding: 1rem 0;
        border-bottom: 1px solid #d2cfc6;
      }

      .evidence-row > div { display: grid; }
      .evidence-row span { font-size: 0.78rem; }

      .research-how,
      .research-privacy {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 0.85fr 1.4fr;
        gap: 4rem;
      }

      .research-steps { display: grid; gap: 1rem; }

      .research-steps article {
        padding: 1.25rem 0;
        border-top: 1px solid #d2cfc6;
      }

      .research-steps span {
        display: inline-block;
        margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
        font-size: 0.8rem;
        font-weight: 800;
        letter-spacing: 0.08em;
      }

      .research-steps h3 { margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-size: 1.4rem; }

      .research-final-cta p:not(.eyebrow) {
        max-width: 760px;
        font-size: 1.15rem;
      }

      @media (max-width: 850px) {
        .big-stats { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
        .research-how, .research-privacy { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
        .evidence-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      }

      @media (max-width: 560px) {
        .research-hero { padding-top: 4rem; }
        .big-stats { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
        .dashboard-heading { align-items: start; flex-direction: column; }
      }
    </style>
  </body>
</html>
